[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd like to propose an addition to <code>SimpleGraph.Metric</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_add_dist_of_lipschitz</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Reachable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With <code>f v = 0</code>, this gives a lower bound on the distance to v, which can be paired with <code>dist_le</code> to prove an exact distance. The proof is a short induction along a shortest walk.</p>\n<p>I used this in my <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-flower formalization to prove lower bounds on distances between cell centers, giving the separation bound needed for the box-counting argument.</p>\n<p>This would also give Manhattan-distance lower bounds for grid graphs with obstacles, or Hamming-distance lower bounds for graphs where each edge flips one bit.</p>",
        "id": 633364020,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792511223
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think some variant of this is probably useful, but I'm not sure which. <code>hf</code> seems a bit specialized to me. For starters, could you generalize beyond <code>ℕ</code>?<br>\nThis reminds me of potential functions in SSSP/APSP problems, and also a bit tangentially <code>prod_map_fstInvMulSnd_darts</code> from <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44958\">#44958</a>, where we're lifting something from edges to walks and everything only depends on the endpoints.</p>",
        "id": 633384057,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792515275
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suspect generalizing too much will give us <code>SimpleGraph.Walk.rec</code>, and without generalizing most uses won't fit this exactly and would prefer to just redo a different short induction proof. Have you found more than one problem where this exact form is useful?</p>",
        "id": 633386194,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792515746
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks. I wasn't sure about <code>hf</code> either, and I appreciate the context. I read <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44958\">#44958</a> and I like the idea of accumulating information from edges along a walk to obtain a statement about its endpoints.</p>\n<p>I tried two more examples that fit the same hypothesis, both with <code>c := 1</code>: integer-graded Hasse graphs with <code>f := grade ℤ</code>, and unit-distance embeddings with <code>f x := dist (ι x) (ι v)</code>. These bound rank differences and ambient distance by walk length, respectively, giving concrete uses for potentials in both <code>ℤ</code> and <code>ℝ</code>.</p>\n<p>We could prove a more general theorem about any walk:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le_add_length_nsmul</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsOrderedAddMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Walk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and derive the distance bound from that.</p>",
        "id": 633392517,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792517135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If we require <code>c</code> to be non-negative we could use <code>dist</code> again I think.<br>\nI'm still not sure about the examples; do you have code examples?</p>",
        "id": 633395801,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792517776
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, we can use <code>G.dist</code> again and use <code>G.Reachable</code>. We can choose a shortest walk, so this version does not need <code>0 ≤ c</code>.</p>\n<p>Here is the lemma with the two rough examples (compiles locally). Both use <code>c = 1</code>, with potentials in <code>ℤ</code> and <code>ℝ</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Hasse</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.UnitDistance.Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Order.Grade</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- An edge bound `f a ≤ f b + c` extends to graph distance without requiring `0 ≤ c`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_add_dist_nsmul</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsOrderedAddMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G.Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G.Reachable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G.dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">obtain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hr.exists_walk_length_eq_dist</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">clear</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nil</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">succ_nsmul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">using</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">add_le_add_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Integer grades give distance lower bounds even when the grading is not bounded below. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grade_le_add_hasse_dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GradeOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hasse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Reachable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">hasse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hasse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rcases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h.grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le.trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le_add_of_nonneg_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_le_one</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Order.covBy_iff_add_one_eq.mp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h.grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ge</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_add_dist_nsmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hr</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- A unit-distance embedding gives geometric lower bounds on graph distance. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UnitDistEmbedding.dist_le_dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MetricSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G.UnitDistEmbedding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G.Reachable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Dist.dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G.dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G.Adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Dist.dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Dist.dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">U.unit_dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_comm</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dist_triangle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">U.p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_add_dist_nsmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hr</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 633406136,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792519830
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"933054\">@Snir Broshi</span> following up. Is the lemma something you'd welcome as a PR?</p>",
        "id": 634530794,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792797256
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well your two examples seem nice, although I wonder if they're provable with some version of the triangle inequality.<br>\nI'm leaning towards yes, but I'd prefer if the PR included a use-case for it.<br>\nThe <code>grade</code> one seems a bit contrived, so maybe the unit-dist one? (or some other one you can think of) Are you sure this is the best way to prove it?<br>\nbtw you're essentially showing <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LipschitzWith#doc\">docs#LipschitzWith</a> for <code>K = 1</code>, although I don't think we have a way to put an <code>EMetricSpace</code> on a graph. Perhaps we should?</p>\n<p>I think there are also lots of ways to generalize the lemma (e.g. <code>edist</code>, <code>length</code> of a given walk, a multiplicative version, <code>Nat.iterate</code> of some function <code>α → α</code> instead of adding a constant, using any <code>IsTrans</code> relation instead of <code>≤</code>) but without a goal to aim for we can't know what forms are actually useful to have.</p>",
        "id": 634534806,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792799638
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, I checked the triangle-inequality approach, and it gives a short proof of the unit-distance result. I don't see an advantage to using this potential lemma there.</p>\n<p>The original motivation was my <a href=\"https://github.com/Project-Navi/fd-formalization/blob/e8c38b26b3e2bac1a2f76ead053ed00ced43a116/FdFormal/FlowerConstruction.lean#L763-L802\">(u,v)-flower formalization</a>. The hubs have natural-number ranks <code>0</code> and <code>u ^ g</code>, and rank changes by at most one across an edge. That gives the distance lower bound, while an explicit walk gives the matching upper bound. Here the potential lemma uses the rank inequalities directly and replaces a local walk induction. The triangle-inequality proof I tried needs extra absolute-value bounds and casts.</p>\n<p>So, that's all I can point to for a use, but my knowledge of mathlib is still limited. Let me look further into <code>EMetricSpace</code> and the suggested generalizations, give me a little bit and I'll report back.</p>",
        "id": 634541183,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792801053
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I ran with your <code>EMetricSpace</code> suggestion and added a <code>MetricVertex G</code> wrapper, keeping the graph metric separate from any existing metric on <code>V</code>.</p>\n<p>For <code>K ≠ 0</code>, checking the bound on edges gives <code>LipschitzWith K</code>. Graph homomorphisms and unit-distance embeddings are then 1-Lipschitz, and the embedding distance bound follows as a corollary. </p>\n<p>Here’s what I have so far: <a href=\"https://github.com/Fieldnote-Echo/mathlib4/commit/658f672d53a94710f6b5546e99ecb7711a30b904\">commit</a>.</p>\n<p>Does this look like a reasonable API?</p>",
        "id": 634545417,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792803309
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's a fine start (though I'd drop <code>lipschitzWith_one_iff</code>; the <code>simpa</code> is faux)<br>\nbut we'd need some motivation to link graphs to metric spaces I think.<br>\nI imagine this will be more sensible once we have graph embeddings and topological graph theory (which is in the works).<br>\nIs there a nice result we can build up to?</p>\n<p>btw does <code>lipschitzWith_iff_of_ne_zero</code> make sense in other metric spaces which aren't graphs? It makes me wonder if some metric spaces could have such a set of pairs that determines whether a function is Lipschitz.<br>\n(edit: apparently not really, but this is related to Menger convexity)</p>",
        "id": 634548377,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792804877
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"933054\">@Snir Broshi</span> Since you asked, my larger research goal is to prove results about continuous limit spaces using finite graph approximations. I see this as a small part of that, which is why I am interested in contributing to the mathlib graph theory API.</p>",
        "id": 634548508,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792804974
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, I'll drop <code>lipschitzWith_one_iff</code>.</p>\n<p>Right now, my larger motivation is a formalization that obtains positive solutions of a nonlinear interval boundary-value problem from finite path-graph solutions, using uniform Lipschitz bounds and Arzelà–Ascoli instead of Schauder estimates.</p>\n<p>The interpolation step might be a useful test case for your idea about determining pairs. Should I open this up in a PR, then we can work out a few follow ups?</p>",
        "id": 634549665,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792805644
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What interpolation step?</p>",
        "id": 634550295,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792806143
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was responding to something in my head there. In my interval proof, I’m joining adjacent node values with straight lines. The edge bounds give a Lipschitz bound independent of mesh size. That’s the connection that came to mind when you asked about a result to build up to.</p>",
        "id": 634550764,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1792806509
    }
]